      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "THE PRICE OF A PROOF",
      "narration_text": "Start with what a proof used to cost. The S.E.L. four kernel took two person-years to write, and twenty to verify: ten times the work. Now the new number. Anthropic says Claude wrote about a hundred and eighty million lines of proof, for two hundred thirty-nine programs, in a few weeks. On average, around seven hundred fifty thousand lines each.",
