    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "TESTS VERSUS A PROOF",
      "narration_text": "Here's the difference. A fuzzer rolls dice: millions of random inputs, hunting for the one that crashes. However many it tries, it only knows about those. A proof is a statement about every input, here up to sixty-four megabytes, made about the compiled program itself, the risk five machine code, and checked by a machine.",
      "shot": {
