      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE RECIPE",
      "narration_text": "The recipe reuses tests people already wrote. Take an OSS-Fuzz test. Compile it to a risk five program. State the theorem: no crash, for any input up to sixty-four megabytes. Claude writes the proof, and the Rocq proof checker verifies it. Nobody reads a hundred million lines. You trust the machine model, the theorem's wording, and the checker.",
